        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ebf01688-60e5-587d-87ac-b1791d5e5f7c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Petit Basset Griffon Vendéen, Toy Trawler Spaniel\n- People: Sara Robertson, Wendy Doherty, Gavin Robertson\n- Organizations: Crufts\n- Places: Vendée, France\n- Concepts: scent hounds, show dogs, extinct breeds\n\nFacts:\n- The Petit Basset Griffon Vendéen, or PBGV, is a dog breed of the scent hound type.\n- The Petit Basset Griffon Vendéen was bred to trail hares in the bramble-filled terrain of the Vendée district of France.\n- The Toy Trawler Spaniel is an extinct breed of Spaniel.\n- The Toy Trawler Spaniel physically resembled the King Charles Spaniel of the 16th century.\n- Soletrader Peek A Boo, also known as Jilly, was a Petit Basset Griffon Vendéen show dog.\n- Soletrader Peek A Boo was owned by Sara Robertson and Wendy Doherty and was handled by Gavin Robertson.\n- In 2013, Soletrader Peek A Boo won Best in Show at Crufts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
